        "type": "text",
        "text": "* climbs the last few steps into the workshop, her red eyes sweeping over the various display racks and storage areas with a satisfied expression *. That sounds perfect, actually - we made good progress last night before... * her gray cheeks warm slightly as she trails off, a fond smile curving her lips *. Yes, before the distraction. * moves toward the alchemy station where she keeps her potion supplies, her fingers brushing along familiar containers *. I think keeping some essentials in the Arch-Mage's quarters makes sense - spare robes, basic supplies, perhaps a few reference texts for when we're working late at the College. But having everything consolidated here... * glances around the workshop with quiet contentment, taking in the space they've made their own *. It feels right, doesn't it? This place has become more *home* than the quarters ever were. * pulls out a small pouch and begins selecting potions - healing, magicka restoration, a stamina draught for good measure *. The quarters are where you work. This is where we *live*. * turns to watch Alethia search for the Staff, her expression soft with affection *. Besides, I've rather been looking forward to seeing all our collected oddities displayed properly. There's something satisfying about organizing months of adventuring into neat, labeled arrangements."
